Bundle-Name: Fennec Services Runtime
Bundle-Description: \
	What a node holds, as a service: the BrokerRuntime and ClientRuntime \
	interfaces with their DTOs, and ChangeCountPublisher, which \
	registers such a service and tells its watchers through \
	service.changecount. \
	\
	Deliberately free of the EMF model. The runtime services describe a \
	node in plain DTOs, and the publisher needs nothing but the \
	framework — so an application that only wants a change-count \
	service installs this bundle and not the model, the fingerprints \
	and the role interfaces with it (#187).

-buildpath: \
	osgi.core;version=latest

# Plain JUnit against a fake BundleContext: the publisher is a thread
# and a registration, and neither needs a framework to exercise.
-testpath: \
	${junit},\
	junit-platform-launcher;version=latest
